--TEST--
an `extend` block may not add an enum under a name its `Core` type already gives an enum: `Core\Arr` has `Core\Arr::Order`, so the block's `enum Order` is the duplicate-declaration error — `rule:classes/an-extend-block-adds-members-to-a-type`
--FILE--
<?nvs
namespace App;

use Core\Arr;

extend Arr as ShopSorting {
    enum Order { Cheapest, Newest }
}

echo "unreachable\n";
// covers: lang:classes/extend-blocks
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0304]: `Core\Arr::Order` is already declared by `Core`
  --> %s:7:10
  |
7 |     enum Order { Cheapest, Newest }
  |          ^^^^^ duplicate declaration
  = help: give the enum a different name. `Core\Arr` already has an enum named `Order`

error: aborting due to 1 error
%A
